im as a man of  questionable morals with a sixth sense  of humor we see only the briefest of  shots featuring the character in the  trailer and he looks sick alright he  appears to be standing in the hall  inside some kind of research facility  most likely the Hawkins National  Laboratory that's connected to all the  town's interdimensional goings-on  he's unkempt with his tie undone smeared  with blood and sporting a twisted smile  his appearance is the first  of several clues which may hint at  Hawkins's big problem this year there  seems to be some kind of infection going  around one which looks to have also  spread to Billy heart row everyone's  least favorite evil stepbrother Lucas's  sister Erica was a comedic bright spot  of stranger thanks to but her role was a  small one this season we're going to  find out a little more about her not the  least of which is the fact that  apparently the prospect of coming  face-to-face with zombified townspeople  and horrific spider looking monsters  doesn't pre-curved in the least in one  shot she's seen commando crawling  through an air duct in full die hard  mode wearing a makeshift miner's helmet  made out of flashlights of tape she only  appeared in four episodes of the second  season but it looks like Erica will be a  little closer to the action this time  around  joining her big brother and his friends  and their unsupervised monster fighting  activities previously released  promotional materials for this season  have leaned heavily on cryptic imagery  and phrases like the line when blue and  yellow meet in the West a phrase which  is turned up in a short teaser trailer  and hidden in Morse code in a  behind-the-scenes book what could this  be referring to there are a couple of  possibilities one shot in the new  trailer features eleven all alone and  wearing a yellow shirt standing on the  beach as an eerie light illuminates the  night sky behind her and to the left is  a blue blue body of water could it be  that a 